From 73a30f994a704202588d01d1cec0fdb1fac5ec6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:48:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] The engine stops uploading the chat tail and diff sidecars
 nothing reads

Two uploads ran for every chat a device hosts, and no client read either:

- the diff sidecar: each checkout's patch, POSTed to {edge}/diff/{chatId}
  for every chat open on it, on every change (diff_sync);
- the tail sidecar: the last 64 messages as JSON, PUT to
  {edge}/chat2/{chatId}/tail on every quiet tick after a change, each one
  materialized on the blocking pool (doc_host's chat2_maintenance).

Checked again: nothing in the engine, zgx, zeron-client, zeron-mobile or
the iOS/Android apps GETs either; the edge stores and serves them
verbatim, and only its smoke scripts read them back. Both are gone, with
what only they used: DiffSidecar, diff_sync's edge config and HTTP client
(CheckoutDiffSync::start* lose their edge argument), zeron-doc's
materialize_tail, SessionTail and TAIL_MESSAGE_COUNT and its test. The
edge routes stay for engines from before. chat2_maintenance keeps the
threshold checkpoint. The tool-output sidecar (upload_tool_sidecar) is
something else and stays. Docs updated.
